course: dictionary
lesson: 12040
title: Circulatory
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Circulatory is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Circulation is the movement of blood round your body. Circulatory is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a system or a problem.
explain: In science, «The circulatory system carries blood to every part of your body.» The system is made of the heart, the blood vessels and the blood. Together they carry oxygen and food to every part of the body and take away waste.
explain: The word can also describe movement in a loop. «The fan made a circulatory flow of warm air around the room.» Here the air moves round in a circle, like a system. Look for clues: is the sentence about blood, the heart or veins? Then it is the body meaning. Is something moving round and round? Then it is the loop meaning.
fact: Circulatory is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like system or problems.
fact: «Circulatory system» means the heart, blood vessels and blood that carry oxygen and food around the body.
fact: Blood vessels include arteries, veins and capillaries.
fact: «Circulatory problems» means problems with blood moving round the body.
fact: In a second sense, circulatory means moving in a circle or loop, like air or water in a system.
exercise: «The circulatory system carries blood to every part of your body.» What does circulatory mean here? | To do with reading and writing | To do with music | *To do with the movement of blood round the body | To do with cold weather
exercise: In «circulatory problems», which word is the noun? | with | *problems | the | circulatory
exercise: «The pump made a circulatory flow of water round the tank.» What does circulatory suggest here? | Frozen solid | *Moving round in a loop | Cold and dry | Moving very fast down a hill
test: Which of these is NOT part of the circulatory system? | Heart | *Bones | Arteries | Veins
test: «Cold fingers can be a sign of circulatory problems.» What does circulatory tell you about the problems? | *They are about blood moving round the body | They are about spelling and grammar | They are about the weather | They are about the eyes
exam: Which sentence uses circulatory correctly to mean blood movement? | The sky was circulatory and blue. | We had circulatory pizza for lunch. | The cat was circulatory on the mat. | *The doctor checked her circulatory system.
